"hadiths[3]{hadithnumber,text}:"
2665,"Narrated to us ‘Īsā ibn Ibrāhīm al-Ghāfiqī, narrated to us Ibn Wahb, who informed me, on the authority of Yūnus, on the authority of Ibn Shihāb, who informed me, on the authority of Sālim ibn ‘Abdullāh ibn ‘Umar (RA), who said:
Ḥafṣah (RA) narrated to me that the Messenger of Allāh (ﷺ) said:
“Five kinds of beasts for which there is no blame upon the one who kills them:
1. The scorpion,
2. The kite (a type of bird of prey),
3. The mouse,
4. The rabid dog,
and
5. The crow.”

**CHAPTER:**"
2666,"Narrated to us Ali bin Abdur-Rahman bin Al-Mughirah Al-Misri, who said: Narrated to us Sa'id bin Al-Hakam, who is the son of Abu Maryam, who said: Inform us Yahya bin Ayoub, from Ibn Ajlan, from Al-Qa'qa' bin Hakim, from Abu Salih, from Abu Hurairah (RA), from the Messenger of Allah (ﷺ), similar to the narration of Al-Layth and Malik, meaning from Nafi', from Ibn Umar ("
2667,"###
 Narrated to us Muhammad ibn Yahya, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Bahar, who said: It was related to me by Hatim, who said: Narrated to us Ibn Ajlan, from Al-Qa'qa', from Abu Salih, from Abu Huraira (RA), who said: The Messenger of Allah (ﷺ) said: ""There are five [animals] whose killing is permissible in the Haram: the snake, the scorpion, the mouse, the kite (bird of prey), and the fierce dog."""
